    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format in `OwnerRestControllerV1.assignCustomerCode` from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to the new `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` format:\n\n- **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the owner's `city`\n- **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the owner's `lastName`\n- **NNNN** \u2014 a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, equal to one more than the number of owners already in that city (replacing the previous global owner count)\n\nThe `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) is derived by concatenating `customerCode`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 no separate change was needed. I updated the method's Javadoc to reflect the new format and example (`SYD-SMI-0007`).\n\nCity matching for the sequence count uses `equalsIgnoreCase`, consistent with the case-insensitive comparisons used elsewhere in the controller. The acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` pattern) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms the suite is green.",
